35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Oh, six weeks lost to weather, and we must pay for off-site rooms for two terms. That is a heavy burden on our schedule and budget.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Wow, specialist rooms are mostly empty, but general ones are always full! We should build what people actually need, not what sits idle.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,The technicians are drowning in manual checks because the old extraction gear fails. We need to fix that burden before adding more work.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The reviews are clear: shared, bookable spaces rated highest, while single-wing projects disappointed. We must prioritize accessibility over isolated benefits.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The plant costs jumped a fifth, and we never set aside a penny to replace the old audio gear. That is a silent tax on our future.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Yumi, your point about usage is wise. But @George, if we fix the extraction, will the technicians finally have some breathing room?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, yes! The data shows general rooms are always full, so we need space people actually use, not just fancy tech.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shizue, yes. The new gear would automate those tedious manual checks, freeing them up. It is the only way to relieve that daily strain.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that relief is vital, but my data shows single-wing projects fail. We need shared, bookable spaces to ensure the investment actually works for everyone.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, shared spaces are fine, but @George, if we ignore the plant cost spike, we are just buying a more expensive problem for next year.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@George, I am glad the new gear helps. But @Mizuki, shared spaces sound lovely, yet I worry about the weather delays and the cost of hiring off-site rooms.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""George"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, I hear you! But the booking data proves general rooms are always full. We need space people actually use, not just fancy tech that sits idle.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Mizuki, I hear your point about shared spaces. But @Benjamin is right; if the plant costs keep climbing, we cannot afford to ignore the maintenance burden on our staff.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Benjamin, the cost spike is real, but @George, the staffing crisis is immediate. We cannot fix the budget by ignoring the people already breaking under the weight.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, the staffing crisis is real, but so is the market. We cannot fix the budget by ignoring the people already breaking under the weight.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Thank you all for sharing. I am worried about the weather delays and the cost of hiring off-site rooms.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I’m still buzzing! The data really shows we need general spaces that are actually used, not just isolated tech. Let’s keep that in mind!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I am glad the data confirms the strain. We must not add more weight to those already carrying the routine upkeep.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,I am glad the data confirms the strain. We must not add more weight to those already carrying the routine upkeep.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I appreciate the sentiment, but empathy does not balance a ledger. We must price the reality, not just the discomfort.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
